Matrix operator regression
==========================

Build DRAMsim3 as described in docs/quick_start.md. From the GEM5 root, build
GEM5 and run one case.

    scons build/RISCV_MATRIX/gem5.opt --default=RISCV --enable-matrix --linker=gold -j64
    python3 .github/workflows/autotest/script/matrix_ci.py run \
        --case rms_norm --output matrix-ci-results

Omit --case to run all 13 operators. The summary is in
matrix-ci-results/validation-results.json. For a failure, open
matrix-ci-results/runs/<case>/sim.log. The exact command is in command.json
in the same directory.

Inputs
------

    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/matrix/*.bin
    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/ref/matrix/riscv64-nemu-interpreter-so

script/matrix_ci.py lists the image filenames. Use --image-dir, --reference
and --gem5 to select other inputs or a different binary. The Matrix REF uses
a 1544-byte register layout.

What CI checks
--------------

gem5-matrix.yml runs on pushes to xs-dev and on manual dispatch. It runs two
cases at a time, with a 30-minute timeout per case, and uploads the logs and
summary as matrix-correctness-results.

Each image must run its optimized xsai-blas operator, match the embedded
reference output and exit normally with difftest enabled. All Matrix commands,
result checks and memory requests must finish. GEMM and FlashAttention must
each report a checked MMA. These two use --classic-l2. The other 11 cases
use the default aligned L2. The large FlashAttention case aborts in
CoherentXBar::recvTimingSnoopResp with the default L2.

Run the result-parser tests with

    python3 -m unittest discover -s .github/workflows/autotest/script -p test_matrix_ci.py
